sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: docs/reference/tasks.md#run-an-external-turn; flow-tighten rule 14. Official SSH and Pi operations remain separate; native assert is the end check.
  %% status: migrated
  %% command: task:turn
  %% kind: tasks.turn
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Task VM<br/>SSH workspace · Pi
  CLI->>GW: task:turn 43<br/> --role=reviewer
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit task:turn 43 --role=reviewer --prompt="Review the checked commit." --thread=new --check=19 --idempotency-key=review-1`
  %%> - syntax: `<task> --role=implementer|reviewer|consult --prompt=TEXT --thread=new|ID [--check=ID] [--json]`
  Note over GW: Admit the turn<br/>owned VM · current child
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - group 42 is external and open; child 43 is current and open
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to the workspace Node
  %%> - the task VM runs; a parked VM is woken by the admission, which records its resume, creates no Operation of this kind and answers `tasks.vm_resuming`; repeat the call once the VM runs
  %%> - a reviewer has an eligible check on the admitted candidate
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - composes the prompt the VM receives: the title, brief and deliverables of the subtask, then the prompt of the caller, for every role
  %%> - records the composed prompt as the admitted intent
  %%> - refuses a composed prompt longer than the workflow accepts, 100000 characters, with `tasks.prompt_too_large`
  %%> Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review:
  %%> - the agent in the VM sees only what the admission sends, so the subtask the Gateway holds reaches it from the Gateway, not from the driver
  opt publication deleted the workspace
    Note over GW: Wait for a task place
    %%> Use the shared first-come-first-served task queue, with a two-hour admission budget. Read the task branch head and admit a fresh VM from the base at that commit, with a new Pi session.
  end
  GW->>SW: Start one run<br/>operation-task-turn
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the admitted prompt, role, session, candidate, SSH identity and vault key names
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>Operation recorded
  %%> Result:
  %%> - follow the Operation while Swamp runs the turn
  opt a fresh task place was admitted
    SW->>N: Claim a task place
    %%> The common task provision child rebuilds the workspace from the base plus the task branch before the turn starts. A failed claim fails the turn and releases its claim.
  end
  Note over SW: prepare
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Build the Pi request and fixed private paths from the admitted intent.
  Note over SW: prepare_local
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Create the private directory for downloaded turn evidence on Node 209.
  SW->>N: prepare_remote
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Create the private snapshot directory in the task VM.
  SW->>N: snapshot_before_index
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Read HEAD into a separate Git index without changing the real index.
  SW->>N: snapshot_before_add
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Include the whole workspace, including unignored untracked files, in that index.
  SW->>N: snapshot_before_head
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Read HEAD before the first Pi send.
  SW->>N: snapshot_before_tree
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Write the exact candidate tree from the separate index.
  Note over SW: snapshot_before
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Validate the HEAD and tree returned by the official SSH operations.
  Note over SW: review_prompt
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - A review-round caller supplies sanitized check evidence. Bind its head to the candidate and its tree to the workspace snapshot, then append it to the Pi prompt.
  %%> - Refuse another head or tree before any Pi send. Other turns keep their prepared prompt.
  SW->>N: receipt_prepare
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Create the agent receipt directory in the checkout.
  SW->>N: receipt_clear
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Remove a stale receipt before sending the new prompt.
  SW->>N: session_create
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Create the admitted Pi session only for a new thread.
  SW->>N: message_send
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Send the admitted prompt once; native resume reuses an accepted send.
  SW->>N: observe
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Flush each complete event into a bounded private transcript file, including before a disconnect or EOF.
  Note over SW: terminal
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Record redacted user/assistant text and tool name, status and duration after success, failure, disconnect or EOF. Tool arguments, outputs and raw errors are discarded.
  %%> - Record usage and nullable cost only from a matching terminal event.
  %%> - Native cancellation skips finalization and keeps the previous recorded transcript.
  SW->>N: snapshot_after_index
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Read HEAD into a separate index after the Pi turn.
  SW->>N: snapshot_after_add
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Include the whole workspace after the turn in that index.
  SW->>N: snapshot_after_head
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Read HEAD after the turn.
  SW->>N: snapshot_after_tree
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Write the resulting workspace tree from the separate index.
  Note over SW: snapshot_after
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Validate the HEAD and tree returned after the turn.
  SW->>N: receipt_exists
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Check whether the agent wrote its receipt.
  SW->>N: receipt_copy
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Download the receipt privately with official SSH copy when it exists.
  SW->>N: difference_counts
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Write the change counts to a private file for a reviewer or consult.
  SW->>N: difference_counts_copy
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Download the private change counts with official SSH copy.
  SW->>N: difference_patch
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Write the workspace patch to a private file for a reviewer or consult.
  SW->>N: difference_patch_copy
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Download the private patch with official SSH copy.
  Note over SW: receipt_read
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Read and redact the downloaded receipt; retain missing or foreign receipt evidence.
  Note over SW: difference
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Read and redact the downloaded change counts and patch for a reviewer or consult.
  SW->>N: interrupt
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Interrupt a turn whose observation failed after an accepted send.
  SW->>N: restore_reset
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Restore the admitted candidate after a reviewer turn.
  SW->>N: restore_clean
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Remove untracked reviewer changes from the checkout.
  SW->>N: restore_head
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Read the restored candidate HEAD.
  SW->>N: restore_tree
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Read the restored workspace tree.
  Note over SW: restore
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Validate the restored candidate identities.
  SW->>N: delete_snapshot_indexes
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Remove completed private snapshot indexes and diff files in the task VM.
  Note over SW: shape_result
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Shape public turn evidence, validate the receipt and retain the producer failure code.
  Note over SW: delete_local_artifacts
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Remove downloaded private artifacts when their readers completed.
  Note over SW: outcome
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Native assert checks the producer result after required cleanup succeeds.
  alt turn and cleanup succeeded
    SW-->>GW: Native terminal result<br/>capture shape_result
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the Gateway captures the complete public producer output in one history read
    Note over GW: Record thread evidence<br/>state · usage · transcript
    %%> Result:
    %%> - record the thread observation without advancing the external group lifecycle
    %%> - a child turn records its evidence as soon as the child ends, while its parent continues
  else turn or cleanup failed
    SW--xGW: Native failed result<br/>failed step · error code
    %%> Result:
    %%> - retain available public evidence and the producer refusal code, including a partial transcript with no usage
    %%> - timeout settlement retains the evidence without reopening the timed-out Operation
    %%> - a cleanup failure keeps the Operation failed even if Pi completed the turn
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - inspect the failed step; native resume reuses the accepted Pi send
  end
  loop until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show<br/>Operation number
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the Operation status and the recorded turn evidence
  end
